          "body_md": "Unlike languages with runtime boundary checks, raw C++ array subscripts `arr[i]` do not throw bounds exceptions. Indexing past buffer boundaries corrupts neighboring stack variables or triggers memory segmentation faults. Always guard access with bounds conditions or employ `std::array::at()` when bounds are dynamically supplied."
