          "id": "T02_1-checkpoint",
          "type": "checkpoint",
          "prompt": "Why does accessing the k-th node in a singly linked list require O(k) time, whereas a dynamic array requires O(1)?",
          "reveal_md": "Array elements occupy contiguous memory, so the CPU computes the target address in O(1) via base + k * sizeof(T). Linked list nodes are scattered across arbitrary heap addresses, requiring the CPU to visit each preceding node sequentially to read its next pointer.",
          "affects_mastery": false
