          "title": "Confusing Worst-Case with Big-O",
          "body_md": "Big-O is a mathematical upper-bounding relation, NOT synonymous with 'worst case'. An algorithm has a best-case Big-O, an average-case Big-O, and a worst-case Big-O. For instance, Quick Sort's best-case time is $O(n \\log n)$, and its worst-case time is $O(n^2)$."
