      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "Consider a Bidirectional Selection Sort (Double Selection Sort) that finds both the minimum and maximum of the unsorted subarray `A[left .. right]` in a single pass and swaps them to `A[left]` and `A[right]`. What subtle bug occurs if the algorithm naively executes `std::swap(A[left], A[minIdx]); std::swap(A[right], A[maxIdx]);` without checking whether `maxIdx == left`?",
