      "answer_explanation": "Pre-call `cout` prints on the way down the recursion (`3 `, then `2 `, then `1 `). `traceBoth(0)` returns immediately. Post-call `cout` prints on the way up as the call stack unwinds in LIFO order (`1 `, then `2 `, then `3 `), producing `3 2 1 1 2 3 `.",
