      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "Consider the naive recursive Fibonacci function:\n```cpp\nint fib(int n) {\n    if (n <= 1) return n;\n    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);\n}\n```\nWhen `fib(5)` is called, how many total function calls to `fib` (including the initial call `fib(5)` and all base-case calls `fib(1)` and `fib(0)`) are executed, and how many times is `fib(2)` evaluated?",
