        "A": "`f2` halves `n` with a single call per step (`Theta(log n)`).",
        "B": "The C++ compiler does not automatically memoize two separate calls `f1(n/2) + f1(n/2)`; both are executed.",
        "D": "Because the argument is `n / 2` (not `n - 1`), branching 2 ways gives `2^(log2 n) = n` calls, not `2^n`."
