      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "To execute sequential sub-tasks `Step 1; Step 2; Step 3;` using a LIFO stack, they must be pushed in reverse order (`Step 3`, then `Step 2`, then `Step 1`). That way `Step 1` is popped and expanded first; once all of `Step 1` finishes, `Step 2` is at the top of the stack; and once `Step 2` finishes, `Step 3` is popped and expanded.",
