      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "What is the auxiliary space complexity of standard top-down Merge Sort on a contiguous array of `n` elements, and why is a single shared pre-allocated buffer `temp[0 .. n-1]` preferred over allocating `new int[right - left + 1]` inside every `merge` call?",
