      "answer_explanation": "Disk and SSD storage have high block-transfer bandwidth for sequential reads/writes, while random seeks across a multi-gigabyte file are orders of magnitude slower. Multiway Merge Sort reads and writes streams sequentially and uses a `k`-way Min-Heap in RAM to merge `k` runs in a single sequential pass.",
