      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "On a sorted or reverse-sorted array, `median(A[low], A[mid], A[high])` is `A[mid]` (the true median.), yielding a perfect `n/2 : n/2` split in `O(1)` overhead. Randomized Quick Sort makes expected time `O(n log n)` over the random coin flips for *every* input array (though deterministic worst-case `O(n log n)` requires either Median-of-Medians `O(n)` selection or Introsort's switch to Heap Sort).",
