      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Unlike Quick Sort (`T(n) = 2T(n/2) + Theta(n) = Theta(n log n)`), Quickselect discards half of the array after partitioning and recurses on only one subproblem: `T(n) = T(n/2) + Theta(n)`. By the geometric series `n + n/2 + n/4 + ... = 2n`, expected time is linear `Theta(n)`. (However, on an unsorted array the first partition alone scans `n` elements, so it is `Theta(n)`, not `O(log n)`).",
