      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "The first node in Preorder (`F`) is always the root. In Inorder, `{A, B, C, D, E}` lie left of `F` (left subtree) and `{G, H, I}` lie right of `F` (right subtree). In the right subtree, Preorder `G, I, H` makes `G` the subtree root; Inorder `G, H, I` puts `{H, I}` in `G`'s right subtree; Preorder `I, H` makes `I` the root of `{H, I}`, and Inorder `H, I` puts `H` as `I`'s left child. Postorder visits `A, C, E, D, B`, then `H, I, G`, then `F`.",
