      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "Every node has 2 outgoing pointer fields (`2n` pointers total). Every node except the root has exactly 1 incoming non-null pointer (`n - 1` non-null pointers). Therefore, the number of `nullptr` child pointers in *any* `n`-node binary tree (balanced or skewed.) is `2n - (n - 1) = n + 1`.",
