      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "If a BST allows duplicate keys (multiset semantics), why is it important to state and enforce a single consistent duplicate-key policy (e.g., *'duplicates go to the right subtree: `left < node <= right`'* or storing a `frequency_count` integer inside each distinct key's node) across `insert`, `search`, and `delete`?",
