      "stem": "In an AVL tree implementation (`ACT_C10_02`), when performing `Node* rotateRight(Node* y)` where `Node* x = y->left;` becomes the new root of the subtree and `y` becomes `x->right`: in what order MUST the cached height fields `y->h` and `x->h` be recomputed after rewiring the pointers?",
