      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "In a B-Tree with minimum degree `t = 3` (`each node holds at most 2t - 1 = 5 keys`), suppose a full child node `y` containing `5` keys `[10, 20, 30, 40, 50]` is split via `B-Tree-Split-Child(x, i)` where parent `x` currently holds `[5, 60]`. What is the state of parent `x` and the two resulting child nodes after the split?",
