        "B": "Connected trees (`E = V - 1`), planar graphs (`E <= 3V - 6`), and bounded-degree networks are connected and sparse.",
        "C": "A connected graph with `V = 10,000` and `E = 20,000` satisfies `E >= V` but has edge density `2E / V^2 ~ 0.0004`—it is extremely sparse."
