      "question_category": "complexity_analysis",
      "stem": "Suppose we want to check whether a specific edge `(u, v)` exists in a graph `G = (V, E)`. What is the worst-case time complexity using a `V x V` Adjacency Matrix `M[u][v]` vs an unsorted Adjacency List `adj[u]`?",
