      "learning_objective_id": "T11_2_LO2",
      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "Consider the following C++ code that reads an undirected weighted graph with `V = 4` vertices and `E = 3` edges into an adjacency list:\n```cpp\nstruct Edge { int to, weight; };\nstd::vector<std::vector<Edge>> adj(4);\nvoid addUndirectedEdge(int u, int v, int w) {\n    adj[u].push_back({v, w});\n    adj[v].push_back({u, w});\n}\n```\nAfter calling `addUndirectedEdge(0, 1, 5); addUndirectedEdge(0, 2, 8); addUndirectedEdge(1, 2, 3);`, what is the total number of `Edge` structs stored across `adj[0]`, `adj[1]`, `adj[2]`, and `adj[3]` combined?",
