      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "A student is implementing a `V x V` Adjacency Matrix for shortest-path algorithms (such as Floyd-Warshall or matrix-based Dijkstra) on a weighted graph where edge weights can be positive or negative, and writes:\n```cpp\nstd::vector<std::vector<int>> mat(V, std::vector<int>(V, 0));\n```\nWhy is initializing every entry `mat[u][v] = 0` for `u != v` a bug, and what is the standard convention?",
