      "question_category": "tradeoff_choice",
      "stem": "If an application needs both `Theta(V + E)` total memory/iteration over neighbors AND expected `O(1)` time for edge-existence queries `(u, v) in E` and edge deletions on a large sparse graph, how can the Adjacency List representation be modified in C++, and what is the trade-off?",
