      "learning_objective_id": "T12_1_LO2",
      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "When BFS is run on a directed graph `G = (V, E)` from source `s`, creating the BFS tree `T_BFS`, which edge types (tree edges, back edges, forward edges, cross edges) can exist in `G` with respect to `T_BFS`, and what constraint holds on `d[u]` and `d[v]` for any directed edge `(u, v) in E`?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Just like undirected BFS, every edge `(u, v)` in a directed BFS graph must connect vertices whose distances differ by at most 1 (`|d[u] - d[v]| <= 1`)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "In a directed BFS tree, there are NO forward edges, while back edges and cross edges can have `d[v]` arbitrarily smaller than `d[u]`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Directed BFS can have forward edges `(u, v)` with `d[v] = d[u] + 3`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Directed BFS cannot have back edges."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "For any directed edge `(u, v)`, when `u` is dequeued at distance `d[u]`, `v` is either already discovered (`d[v] <= d[u] + 1`) or discovered right then (`d[v] = d[u] + 1`). Thus `d[v] <= d[u] + 1` always holds, ruling out any forward edge (which would require `v` to be a proper non-child descendant with `d[v] >= d[u] + 2`). However, because `(u, v)` is one-way, a back edge `(u, s)` from level `d[u] = 10` back to `s` (`d[s] = 0`) is completely possible.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "In a *directed* graph, an edge `(u, s)` from a vertex at distance `d[u] = 5` back to the root `s` (`d[s] = 0`) has `d[u] - d[s] = 5 > 1` because `(u, s)` is one-way (`s` could not traverse `(u, s)` backward).",
        "C": "Any direct edge `(u, v)` guarantees `d[v] <= d[u] + 1`, so `d[v] = d[u] + 3` is impossible.",
        "D": "Any directed cycle reachable from `s` produces at least one back edge or cross edge."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "hard",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "MC_DIRECTED_BFS_EDGE_CLASSIFICATION"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://opendsa-server.cs.vt.edu/ODSA/Books/Catalog/html/index.html",
        "https://cp-algorithms.com/graph/breadth-first-search.html"
      ],
