      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "When using DFS to detect whether an undirected simple graph contains a cycle, why must `dfs(int u, int parent)` pass the immediate `parent` vertex and check `if (v == parent) continue;` before declaring an already-visited neighbor `v` to be a back edge?",
