      "question_family_id": "QF_T12_2_F08",
      "concept_id": "C12",
      "topic_id": "T12_2",
      "learning_objective_id": "T12_2_LO3",
      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "By the White-Path Theorem, in any DFS forest of a (directed or undirected) graph `G = (V, E)`, vertex `v` becomes a descendant of vertex `u` in the DFS tree if and only if, at the exact time `d[u]` when `u` is discovered:",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`v` is a direct neighbor of `u` (`(u, v) in E`) and `v` is `WHITE`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "There is *any* directed path from `u` to `v` in `G` (regardless of vertex colors at time `d[u]`)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "There is a path from `u` to `v` in `G` consisting entirely of `WHITE` vertices."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "The shortest path from `u` to `v` has fewer edges than the shortest path from the root to `v`."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "The White-Path Theorem states that `v` is a descendant of `u` in the DFS forest iff at time `d[u]` there exists a path from `u` to `v` consisting solely of `WHITE` vertices. If every path from `u` to `v` is blocked by an already-visited (`GRAY` or `BLACK`) vertex `w`, `DFS-Visit(u)` cannot pass through `w` to reach `v`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Descendants include indirect grandchildren/great-grandchildren along any all-white path, not just direct neighbors.",
        "B": "Consider `0 -> 1 -> 2` and `0 -> 2` where `0` visits `2` *first* (`2` turns `BLACK`), and then `0` visits `1`: there is a path `1 -> 2`, yet `2` is NOT a descendant of `1` because `2` was already `BLACK` at time `d[1]`.",
        "D": "DFS tree membership depends on discovery order and white paths, not shortest-path hop counts."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "hard",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "MC_WHITE_PATH_THEOREM"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://opendsa-server.cs.vt.edu/ODSA/Books/Catalog/html/index.html",
        "https://cp-algorithms.com/graph/depth-first-search.html"
      ],
      "verification_method": "source_cross_check",
      "agent_check_status": "passed",
