      "answer_explanation": "Even though asymptotic space is `O(V)`, each C++ call frame uses 32–64+ bytes on the OS thread stack. At depth `200,000`, `~10+ MB` of call stack can overflow an `8 MB` default stack limit (`ulimit -s`), whereas heap-allocated `std::vector` / `std::stack` uses gigabytes of available RAM safely.",
