      "stem": "Trace Kahn's Algorithm using a standard FIFO queue (initially pushing `indegree == 0` vertices in ascending vertex ID order) on the graph with `V = 5` vertices `{0, 1, 2, 3, 4}` and edges:\n`0 -> 2`, `1 -> 2`, `1 -> 3`, `2 -> 4`, `3 -> 4`.\nWhat are the initial in-degrees `indegree[0..4]`, and in what exact order are vertices popped from the queue?",
