        "A": "Using `std::min` would let a course `v` be taken as soon as *one* of its prerequisites finished, even while another deeper prerequisite chain for `v` wasn't finished yet.",
        "C": "Multiple independent courses can be taken in the *same* semester (`sem = 1`), whereas their indices in a 1D topological array are all distinct.",
        "D": "Summing `sem[u]` adds parallel prerequisite chains together instead of taking the bottleneck maximum."
