      "stem": "In C++, a student initializes `std::vector<int> dist(V, INT_MAX);` (`INT_MAX = 2,147,483,647`) and writes the relaxation check:\n```cpp\nif (dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {\n    dist[v] = dist[u] + w;\n}\n```\nWhat critical C++ bug occurs when `u` has not yet been reached (`dist[u] == INT_MAX`) and `w > 0`?",
