      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "Consider the directed graph on 3 vertices `{0, 1, 2}` with edges:\n`0 -> 1 (w = 4)`, `0 -> 2 (w = 5)`, and `2 -> 1 (w = -3)` (note: this is a DAG with no cycles, so no negative-weight cycle exists.).\nWhy does standard Dijkstra's Algorithm (which finalizes each vertex on its first pop from the priority queue and never re-expands finalized vertices) fail to find the shortest path to vertex `1` from source `0`?",
