      "learning_objective_id": "T12_5_LO3",
      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "How does the Bellman-Ford Algorithm compute single-source shortest paths from `s` on a general weighted directed graph `G = (V, E)` (which may have negative edge weights), why does its main loop run `V - 1` iterations, and what is its worst-case time complexity?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "It uses a priority queue to relax edges in `O((V + E) log V)` time."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "It runs `E` passes relaxing `V` edges per pass, because a simple shortest path in a `V`-vertex graph can contain up to `E` distinct edges."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "It sorts the `E` edges by weight and relaxes each edge once in `O(E log E)` time."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "It runs `V - 1` passes relaxing all `E` edges per pass; since any simple shortest path without negative cycles has at most `V - 1` edges, the Path-Relaxation Property guarantees `dist[v] == delta(s, v)` after `V - 1` passes in `O(V * E)` time."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "D",
      "answer_explanation": "Any shortest simple path `s = v_0 -> v_1 -> ... -> v_k = v` has `k <= V - 1` edges (`k + 1 <= V` distinct vertices). Since pass `1` relaxes `(v_0, v_1)`, pass `2` relaxes `(v_1, v_2)`, and pass `i` relaxes `(v_{i-1}, v_i)`, by the Path-Relaxation Property, `dist[v_k]` is guaranteed to converge to the true shortest-path distance after at most `k <= V - 1` passes.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Using a priority queue is Dijkstra's algorithm, not Bellman-Ford.",
        "B": "Any walk with `>= V` edges must repeat a vertex (forming a cycle); if no negative cycle exists, removing cycles leaves a simple path of `<= V - 1` edges.",
        "C": "Relaxing edges only once in sorted weight order fails whenever a shortest path uses a heavy edge before a light edge."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "MC_BELLMAN_FORD_V_MINUS_ONE_PASSES_REASON"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
