      "learning_objective_id": "T12_5_LO3",
      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "Suppose a directed graph `G = (V, E)` contains a negative-weight cycle `C`, but `C` lies in a component that is NOT reachable from the source vertex `s` (`dist[u] == INF` for all `u in C`). What will a single-source Bellman-Ford run from `s` (which guards relaxations with `if (dist[u] != INF)`) report, and how do we modify the setup if we want to detect whether `G` contains a negative-weight cycle anywhere in the entire graph?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Bellman-Ford from `s` only detects negative cycles reachable from `s`; to detect a negative cycle anywhere in `G` in `O(V * E)` time, set `dist[v] = 0` for all `v in V`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Single-source Bellman-Ford from `s` with `dist[v] = INF` (`v != s`) already detects all negative cycles in `G` even in components unreachable from source `s`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Detecting a negative cycle that is unreachable from `s` is never able to be done in `O(V * E)` time and requires running Bellman-Ford `V` separate times in `O(V^2 * E)` time."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Setting `dist[v] = 0` for all `v in V` causes false-positive negative cycle reports on positive-weight cycles."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "With `if (dist[u] != INF)` and `dist[v] = INF` for `v != s`, unreachable vertices remain at `INF` forever and are never relaxed. Setting `dist[v] = 0` for all `v in V` corresponds to a virtual source `S^*` connected to every vertex with a `0`-weight edge (from which every cycle in `G` is reachable, and since `S^*` has no incoming edges, no new cycles are created.), detecting any negative cycle in `G` in a single `O(V * E)` run.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "B": "If `dist[u] == INF` on an unreachable cycle, `if (dist[u] != INF)` skips those edges on all `V` passes.",
        "C": "The virtual super-source trick (`dist[v] = 0` for all `v`) solves global negative-cycle detection in a single `O(V * E)` run.",
        "D": "Positive-weight cycles never decrease `dist[v]` below `0`."
      },
