        "C": "Dijkstra can fail on negative-weight DAGs (Scenario 2), and Prim computes an MST, not shortest paths (Scenario 3).",
        "D": "`O(V * E)` is `Theta(V^2)` on sparse graphs, orders of magnitude slower than `O(V + E)` or `O((V + E) log V)` when structure permits."
