      "question_category": "complexity_analysis",
      "stem": "In a complete graph `K_n` with `n` cities (`n >= 3`), if we fix city `0` as the starting point of the tour to eliminate cyclic shifts, how many distinct directed Hamiltonian tours `(0, pi_1, pi_2, ..., pi_{n-1}, 0)` exist (and how many undirected tours if edge costs are symmetric), and why is brute-force enumeration infeasible for `n = 25`?",
