      "stem": "A student implements Nearest-Neighbor TSP in C++ and returns `total_cost` after the `n - 1` greedy steps (`for (int step = 0; step < n - 1; ++step)`) without adding `dist[cur][start]` at the end. What graph object has the student actually computed instead of a TSP tour?",
