      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Because Local Search only inspects solutions inside the local neighborhood `N(s)` (e.g., 2-Opt swaps), it stops as soon as `f(s) <= f(s')` for all `s' in N(s)`. If reaching a better tour requires changing `3` or `4` edges simultaneously while every single `2`-edge swap increases cost, `s` is trapped in a local minimum that is not globally optimal.",
