      "answer_explanation": "Once `T^*` is a 2-Opt local minimum, every 2-Opt neighbor has `cost >= cost(T^*)`. To find a better solution, you must either jump to a different basin of attraction (random restarts / Iterated Local Search kicks), expand the neighborhood (`3-Opt` checks triples of edges so a `2-Opt` local minimum may have an improving `3-Opt` neighbor.), or temporarily allow uphill moves (Simulated Annealing / Tabu Search).",
