      "answer_explanation": "Apply the definitions directly:\n1. Forward edges (`u in S = {s, a}`, `v in T = {b, t}`) are `(a, b)` and `(s, b)`, so `c(S, T) = c(a, b) + c(s, b) = 10 + 5 = 15`.\n2. Backward edge (`v in T, u in S`) is `(b, a)` with `f(b, a) = 3`, so `f(S, T) = (f(a, b) + f(s, b)) - f(b, a) = (8 + 4) - 3 = 9` (and notice `|f| = f(S, T) = 9 <= 15 = c(S, T)`.).",
