      "learning_objective_id": "T15_1_LO3",
      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "By the Weak Duality of network flows (Flow Across Any Cut), for any valid flow `f` and any `s-t` cut `(S, T)` in `G`, how does the net flow `f(S, T)` relate to the flow value `|f|` and the cut capacity `c(S, T)`?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Equality `|f| == c(S, T)` holds across a cut `(S, T)` if and only if both forward edges in `S x T` and backward edges in `T x S` are saturated (`f == c`)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Net flow `f(S, T)` equals `|f|` only when `(S, T)` is a minimum cut; for non-minimum `s-t` cuts, `f(S, T)` is strictly greater than `|f|`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "For every `s-t` cut `(S, T)`, net flow satisfies `f(S, T) == |f| <= c(S, T)`, with equality `|f| == c(S, T)` if and only if every forward edge `(u, v) in S x T` is saturated and every backward edge `(v, u) in T x S` has zero flow."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "The flow value `|f|` can be strictly greater than the cut capacity `c(S, T)` whenever the directed network `G` contains cycles crossing `(S, T)`."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "By summing the flow-conservation identity (`net outflow(u) == 0`) over all `u in S \\ {s}` and adding `net outflow(s) = |f|`, all internal edges `(x, y) in S x S` cancel out in pairs, leaving `|f| = f(S, T)` for every `s-t` cut `(S, T)`. Then:\n`|f| = f(S, T) = sum_{S->T} f(u, v) - sum_{T->S} f(v, u) <= sum_{S->T} c(u, v) - 0 = c(S, T)`.\nEquality holds iff `f(u, v) = c(u, v)` on all `S -> T` edges and `f(v, u) = 0` on all `T -> S` edges.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Any positive flow `f(v, u) > 0` on a backward edge `T -> S` *subtracts* from `f(S, T)`, so saturation of `(S, T)` requires `f(v, u) == 0` on all `T -> S` edges.",
        "B": "`f(S, T) == |f|` is a conservation identity that holds for *every* `s-t` cut `(S, T)` and *every* valid flow `f`.",
        "D": "Weak duality `|f| <= c(S, T)` is an absolute mathematical upper bound for all flows and all cuts."
      },
