      "learning_objective_id": "T15_1_LO2",
      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "In practical C++ implementations of Max Flow (such as Edmonds-Karp or Dinic's algorithm), how do we represent the residual network so that whenever we augment flow along an edge `e = (u, v)` by `+Delta`, we can update both its forward residual capacity (`-= Delta`) and its paired reverse edge's residual capacity (`+= Delta`) in `O(1)` time?",
