      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "In standard flow network definitions, if a directed graph contains antiparallel edges (both `(u, v)` and `(v, u)` present in `E` with positive capacities `c_1` and `c_2`), how can antiparallel edges be eliminated without changing the maximum flow, and why is this handled automatically in the twin-edge adjacency-list (`idx ^ 1`) code representation?",
